  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "mtp-data-local-mutex-init-and-common-cleanup",
      "category": "synchronization_and_lifetime",
      "severity": "NO_UNBALANCED_INIT_OR_FREE_CONFIRMED; CONDITIONAL_DEVM_RELEASE_GAP_REMAINS",
      "disposition": "ALL_FOUR_JOERN_ALERTS_CLASSIFIED; STOCK_CONTROL_FLOW_PRESERVED",
      "details": "Both local mutexes are initialized after parameter validation and before the flash helpers receive their contexts. Every path after initialization reaches the common cleanup, including setup/read errors and success. The two devm_kfree operations are guarded by a fresh managed-device lookup; if that lookup returns NULL, the pointer is then cleared without an immediate free. The same conditional cleanup appears in Ghidra stock. This is a conditional retained-devres risk during a device-lifecycle interleaving; static evidence did not establish that the provider returns NULL after these allocations, and no runtime detach race was modeled. The MTP config buffer is zero-initialized and this call does not exercise the helper’s existing-buffer resize path.",
