    {
      "id": "mtp-config-buffer-resize-conditional-old-buffer-retention",
      "category": "lifetime",
      "severity": "CONDITIONAL_OLD_DEVM_BUFFER_CAN_BE_ABANDONED",
      "disposition": "INHERITED_STOCK_BEHAVIOR; HARDENING_REQUIRES_SEPARATE_DEVIATION",
      "details": "When buffer->data is already non-NULL and too small, the helper queries the managed device before freeing it. If that lookup returns NULL, the code retries; if the retry also returns NULL it clears buffer->data and returns, and if the retry succeeds it overwrites buffer->data with a new allocation. In either branch the old devm allocation is not immediately freed and remains attached to devres until device teardown. The repository caller is syna_tcm_read_flash_area, which accepts a caller-owned tcm_buffer; the exact conditions are present in Ghidra stock and stock assembly. Whether detach can produce this interleaving for a live call was not demonstrated. The MTP caller uses a fresh zeroed buffer, so this resize case is not triggered by syna_tcm_read_mtp_data itself.",
